    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="1069" n="963" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg963"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760m.6111/31: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-10T17:00:00+03:00">October 10, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 10—1:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>721. My telegram 673, October 4, 2 p.m. Although no announcement thereof has
                    appeared in the Soviet press, I understand that in addition to the meeting
                    reported in my telegram under reference the Lithuanian delegation had further
                    conferences in the Kremlin on the following day. The Commander-in-Chief of the
                    Lithuanian Army<anchor n="47" xml:id="d774-f1"/> and the Vice Premier left for
                    Kaunas yesterday morning and are expected back today. The Lithuanian Foreign
                    Minister and the other delegates have remained in Moscow. I have been unable to
                    ascertain <pb facs="1070" n="964" xml:id="pg964"/> the reasons for the delay in
                    the conclusion of a Lithuanian-Soviet agreement but I believe the delay has
                    resulted from enlarged Soviet demands.</p>
                <p>Repeated to the Legation at Kaunas.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
